WEBVTT

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.700
Ushiku-san!

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.440
Maybe you didn't see me! It's me!

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.680
Of course I see you!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.380
I'm ignoring you because you embarrass me!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.560
Get off of me!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.000
<b>Club Application
Club name (Association name)
Class | Name</b>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.020
<b>Anima Yell!</b>

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.760
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.310
<b>Episode 09: The Captain Is Chosen! Five-Person Cheer Squad</b>

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.760
And so...

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.970
Welcome to the cheer association!

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.620
Welcome, Ushiku-san.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.700
You didn't have to come get me. 
I could've come here myself.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.660
More importantly, Sawatari-san, 
how's your leg?

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.240
Oh, it's fine.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.150
I'm totally better after some rest.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.790
You're so nice, Ushiku-san. 
You were worried about Uki.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.370
W-Well, I mean, I'm partially responsible...

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.330
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:28.040
Ushiku-san, you're already here?

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.520
You're a bit late. Did something come up?

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.250
Well, I stopped by Ushiku-san's classroom...

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.130
I'm so sorry I'm here! You even went 
to the trouble of going to my class!

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.190
Talk about a difference in attitude!

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.280
Okay, let's get that club 
application taken care of!

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.090
Here!

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.080
Do I have to write my full name?

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.300
Yup!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.690
<i>She's hesitating to write her name...</i>

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.940
<i>Does that mean Ushiku-san also</i>

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.660
<i>has a name that's not very girly?</i>

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.320
Ushiku Hanawa

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.370
I don't think you should get 
people's hopes up like that.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.370
[Hana means flower]

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.450
Huh? Did I do something bad?

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.670
Ushiku Hanawa-chan!

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.080
Yes, Hanawa-san.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.080
No!

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.840
I knew you were going to say that!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.210
It's Kana! Don't call me Hanawa.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:23.080
Hanawa... But that sounded so joyous.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.090
<b>Congratulations</b>

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.090
<b>Open</b>

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.510
<i>Joyous? A nose ring (hanawa) sounds joyous?</i>

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.810
Joyous

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:32.140
I-If you say so, Senpai...

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:38.010
Okay, you're our fifth member, Hanawa-chan! 
Welcome to the cheer association!

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.800
Don't call me Hanawa!

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.840
Aw, but it sounds so cute...

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.450
Only Senpai can call me that.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.100
Fifth member?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.260
Wait, a fifth member means...

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.080
Yes.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.010
Five members...

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.920
That means we need to choose our colors!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.020
I choose orange!

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.440
We're not on some sentai show!

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.630
Also, who chooses orange?!

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.970
It means we can become a club now.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.130
Oh, right. Because we have five members now.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.890
We can finally become a club!

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.820
We can go from being the cheer 
association to being the cheer club!

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.350
Yay! We're finally the cheer club!

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.940
We did it, Kohane-chan.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.960
Hey, how are an association and 
a club different, anyway?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:18.970
No idea!

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.900
After you got that excited?!

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:25.630
The big changes are that we get a 
club room, advisor, and club funds.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.410
President    Advisor    Club Room

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.220
Club funds? They're giving us money?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.250
But the timing might not 
be too great right now.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.790
The first semester ends soon, 
so it might have to wait

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.480
until after the second semester's 
club presidents' meeting.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.900
So starting in the second semester, 
we'll be living on easy street!

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.460
Er... You just keep dreaming big, kid.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.970
<b>President</b>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.320
Right! And now we have a club president!

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.970
I guess that'd naturally be Hizume.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:48.460
Yes.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.460
No, I think you should do it, Kohane-san.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.710
S-Senpai, if you say so, then...

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:57.730
Then...

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.480
<i>Her resistance is winning.</i>

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.610
Kohane-san has the ability to give others 
a slight push and help them move forward.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.500
I think that's a perfect fit for a 
cheer club president and captain.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.580
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.830
Kotecchan, Hizume...

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.250
I mean, her methods are a bit...

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.710
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.340
Wait.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.840
But you'll have to go to presidents' meetings

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.520
and negotiate for club funds and the like.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.090
Are you really up to that task?

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.470
Kohane going to a meeting...

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:35.960
Um... Could I have some club funds?

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.750
Please?

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.300
I'm so tired.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.350
But I have to bring back some club funds!

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.630
She'd be cute, so I think it'd be okay.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.070
I don't think Kohane-chan's <i>that</i> young.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.480
If we get club funds,

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:55.310
we'll be able to put them toward 
cheer supplies and equipment.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.210
Oh, yeah!

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.080
We've just been buying them ourselves 
or making them up until now.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:03.520
But our current uniforms are handmade...

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.520
Right. So Kana-chan will
have to make her own, too.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.760
Huh? I do? I have to sew it by hand?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.970
Don't worry! We have patterns!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.050
This is Uki's pattern!

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.110
A ghost?!

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.980
Why do you have that, Kohane?!

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.630
I think we can just use our current 
room as a club room for now.

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.050
That just leaves the advisor.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.760
Since you're like an honor student,

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.440
aren't you close with any teachers?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.110
No, I can't say that I am.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.860
Hey, I think I know someone.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.900
Kohane-chan, you see, an advisor is a teacher
who'll watch over the club's activities.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:38.370
Huh? Oh, yeah. I know that.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.920
<b>Faculty Room</b>

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.920
And so...

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.070
The cheer club finally has five members.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.380
Will you be our advisor, Inukai-sensei?

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.500
Cheerleading gives you a lot of energy,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.340
so I think it'd be perfect for you, 
since you always seem so exhausted.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:54.160
I do seem exhausted, which is exactly 
why I'd rather not be your advisor.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.710
We have an electric pot and 
snacks in our club room,

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.250
so you can have all the tea breaks you want!

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.140
Kohane! Don't say that 
in front of a teacher!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.270
Tea? Then...

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.640
Do you happen to have a massage chair?

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.110
You really are exhausted.

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.590
But I don't know a thing about cheerleading.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.550
You're okay with that?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:12.820
That's fine!

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.010
I only learned after
I started at this school!

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:16.540
Right?

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.880
Yeah. We only started in spring, 
and it was a bit difficult at first,

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.040
but I definitely feel stronger now.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.380
I... lack stamina,

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.210
and if someone asked, 
I'm not exactly that good...

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.200
More importantly,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.690
I'm still worried that I might 
be inconveniencing everyone.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:37.850
I mean, should I really be cheerleading?

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.300
What are we actually doing for cheerleading?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.560
Hey... You're wandering 
off-course over there.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.430
But I'm sure you'll fall in 
love with cheer, Sensei!

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:49.820
I'm not so sure about that.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.050
Well, cheerleading is a 
very appealing sport.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:53.700
Yeah!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.950
Not to mention, the other day when 
I was helping Kumagai-sensei...

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:05.040
She said that in middle school, you were 
called Interpretive Dance Inukai!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.920
<b>I am...</b>

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.920
<b>a dandelion...</b>

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.650
Oh... She must be talking 
about another Inukai-san.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.300
But...

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.470
<b>Childhood friends with Inukai-sensei</b>

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.340
She said she even had a DVD.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.590
Okay, fine! I'll be your advisor!

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:18.810
Kids are so scary these days!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.430
Yay! We'll work really hard 
so you end up liking cheer!

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:25.690
We'll cheer all your fatigue away!

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.170
Okay, okay, I get it, Hatoya.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.710
I'll even massage your shoulders for you!

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:30.970
Ow, ow! Ow!

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.360
She might actually be a good president.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.400
Who knew she was this talented?

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:39.550
Now then, this means 
that the cheer association

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:42.240
is now officially the cheerleading team.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.060
And you've already got a request.

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.250
What? Again?

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.630
Apparently, one of the parents saw you

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.920
cheering for the basketball 
team the other day.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.120
That's great! It's all starting to connect!

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.480
Our cheerleading circle's 
growing even bigger!

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:58.590
Now someone else might see our 
cheering and make another request.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:01.120
And that might even create 
another opportunity.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:01.770
Yeah!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.440
It's a request for you to cheer 
at a grade school soccer match

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.270
and do a halftime performance.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.420
The team you'll be cheering 
for is called the Victories.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.020
Huh?!

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:12.970
Let's stop these connections for a bit.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:14.030
Why?!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.720
Wait, this soccer team...

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:19.410
Victories
Request for the cheer club to cheer at a soccer game

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:19.020
Uki, are you still...

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.660
Still what?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.020
Are you still on that team or something?

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.040
Of course I'm not!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.890
Maybe there's someone 
you still can't forget...

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.420
A grade schooler?

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:33.450
Still what, then?

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.760
S-Still... Still...

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:39.280
Still haven't fulfilled your 
dream of going to Madagascar!

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.470
<i>Thanks for that extinction-level cover-up.</i>

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.860
I'm not sure what's going on,

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.920
but you're okay with accepting
this request, right?

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.760
Oh, um...

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:49.550
We want to accept, but...

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:53.110
Oh, yeah! You can totally accept! Go ahead!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:57.740
Victories
Request for the cheer club to cheer at a soccer game
Riverbed Soccer Field

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.940
So your little brother is on 
this soccer team, Uki-chan?

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:57.740
Yeah...

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.440
Then that's even more of 
a reason to cheer them on.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:02.810
Opportunities like this don't come up often.

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:09.350
But Akane really hates girly things lately,

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.750
Uki Akane

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.750
Third Grade

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.750
so I haven't told him I'm cheerleading.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:15.040
So what club does he think you're in?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.380
Th-The track team along with Kohane.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:19.000
Really?

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.010
I'm not sure how convincing that is...

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.660
You guys all told your families?

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:24.520
Yeah.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.290
Senpai and I needed permission 
from our guardians

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:29.280
to even be on the local squad.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.580
I originally started cheerleading 
to cheer for my older brother.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:34.900
You did?!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:40.160
Senpai's older brother... 
He must be a person of integrity!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.440
Yes. My brother is someone 
you can look up to.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:45.040
I'm very proud of him.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.430
I knew it!

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.850
Um... I wouldn't take that too seriously.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:52.910
Misconceptions happen all the time.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:54.130
Huh? What?

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.350
So what did your brother do?

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:57.020
He—

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:58.090
Hey, wait a sec!

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.560
I need to prepare myself so I'm ready 
for whatever you're about to say.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.580
Just what do you think my brother is?

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:05.820
He did kendo.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.600
That's so normal!

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:11.000
It was a very simple motive of making 
him happy by cheering for him, but...

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.020
Sounds great!

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.700
I'm sure Akane-kun will be happy, too!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.540
Y-You think so?

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:18.670
Maybe he'll even start cheerleading!

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:19.530
Huh?

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:23.550
Why not? There are a lot more 
guys doing cheerleading lately.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:27.240
Yeah, but... Him quitting soccer 
for cheerleading would be a bit...

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:31.290
It's all right. They're only 
interested in the very beginning.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:37.960
I wonder if he'd actually be happy.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.430
I'm home.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:44.680
Oh, hey. Welcome home... 
wait, what's wrong, Akane?

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:48.430
Some random girls came to 
cheer us on at practice.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.060
Their screeching was so 
loud that it was distracting!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.160
What's wrong, Sis?

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.320
O-Oh, nothing...

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.700
<i>He's definitely not going 
to be happy about this.</i>

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:05.130
Ugh... Why do girls have 
such annoying voices?

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.660
I'm just trying to concentrate 
on soccer practice.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.670
<i>Jeez... talk about the 
worst possible timing.</i>

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.410
<i>I can't bring myself to tell him.</i>

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.310
<i>But he's going to find out anyway,</i>

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.880
<i>so I might as well tell him 
sooner rather than later.</i>

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:21.370
S-Say, Akane...

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:25.370
Oh! You're, I mean... 
You're not the same as them.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.810
You're not obnoxious, and you're cool.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.100
You're in a club for running, right?

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:34.860
Could you teach me the trick 
to running faster sometime?

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:39.070
Sis? Sis?!

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.440
<b>Includes diagrams for quick results!
The Trick to Running Faster
Running Fast for Dummies!</b>

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:42.700
So that's why you're reading 
a book about running?

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.190
You're pathetic.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:47.450
Just look him in the eyes and tell him.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:50.490
Isn't that what I told you the other day?

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.720
Why don't you just come out and say it?

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:58.080
If she could do that, she'd probably 
have already mentioned the cheer club.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.420
Not to mention, it's not the 
easiest thing to bring up.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.790
Then why don't you just let 
him see you in your uniform

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.880
and figure it out that way?

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:09.510
See me in my uniform?

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:12.890
I-I'm home...

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.270
Your face is a little red. Are you okay?

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.420
Why did you wear it under 
your school uniform?

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:22.680
That's pointless.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.460
W-Well...

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:27.660
I think he'd get it if you 
did a cheer in front of him.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.110
Hey! I can do one with you!

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:31.540
Please don't!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.320
Yes!

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:37.620
I'm home!

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.410
You scared me! You're being too loud, Sis!

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.580
And "yes" what?

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:46.820
Oh, uh... I was just 
reviewing some English...

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.130
Fail

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.890
While I was busy doing all this crap...

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.390
The match is tomorrow!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.880
At this point, I think

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:57.820
he'll automatically find out tomorrow 
without you doing anything.

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:01.770
It's different telling him beforehand 
and having him find out on the spot!

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:04.380
Then you'll just have to tell him tonight.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.820
But if you tell him early, 
he might skip the match.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:08.780
Akane would never

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.740
skip a match over something like that...

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.160
I don't... think...

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.290
Uki! Your face!

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:20.090
Hey... You're playing in your 
match tomorrow, right, Akane?

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.280
Yeah, of course I am.

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:25.980
I-I'm thinking of coming 
by to cheer you on.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:27.470
Huh?! You don't have to!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.880
The other kids said their 
families weren't coming,

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.200
so don't come, no matter what! You got it?

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.350
I'm serious!

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:39.610
Speaking of cheering, I guess some 
cheerleaders are coming tomorrow.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:41.870
R-Really? That sounds nice.

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:43.840
I'm sure they'll liven up the game.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:44.730
It's not nice at all!

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:48.490
I don't like it.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.610
I mean, they're just fooling around!

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.130
Showing off their p-panties 
when they're dancing...

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.560
They're all flashy and stuff!

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.800
I just want to play soccer seriously.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.890
Cheerleading is so embarrassing.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.700
Wait. How did you know 
about the match tomorr—

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.010
What did you just say?

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:06.590
Huh?

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:10.380
Flashy? Showing off their 
panties while they're dancing?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.970
Where are you even looking, you perv?

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.120
Huh? Perv?

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:16.720
That's not what cheerleading's about!

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.440
Make sure you keep those pervy 
eyes wide open tomorrow!

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.730
You'll see what real cheerleading is!

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.560
Sis?

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:29.310
Thank goodness you were able 
to tell him the day before!

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.570
Looks like it went great!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.480
I just treated my little 
brother like a perv...

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.940
And then I had the nerve to 
show up in skimpy clothes...

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.210
You're going to prove

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:43.960
that he was wrong, right?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.720
Let's go.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.960
I hope your brother will be there!

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:52.340
You just don't know when to stop, do you?

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.970
We're the Kaminoki High 
School Cheerleading Squad.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.130
Thanks for having us today.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.510
It's a pleasure to have you. 
Thanks for coming.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:03.980
Sis?!

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:05.480
And Kohane!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.160
Akki's older sister?

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.280
Wait, which one is she?

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.910
Sh-She's not my sister! Stop looking!

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.040
Stop looking!

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.460
<i>Am I that embarrassing to look at?</i>

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:16.870
Akane...

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:19.420
I'm sorry I kept this a secret.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.680
Do your best today.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.120
Whatever.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.000
I'm not even a starter, anyway.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:29.500
Okay.

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.300
Then let's see who can cheer the best!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:35.930
See who's the best?!

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.430
Hizume-chan, I don't think it's 
as serious as you're making it.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:44.190
<i>What the heck, Sis?</i>

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:48.150
<i>Why are you wearing something 
so cute— I mean, flashy?</i>

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:50.760
You can do—

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:52.440
Go, Victories, go!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.460
Go, Victories, go!

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:56.490
Go, Victories, go!

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:57.780
Everyone!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.640
Go, Victories, go!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.270
Let's make our voices heard!

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.670
Go, Victories, go!

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:02.400
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:03.040
Go, Victories, go!

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:03.040
Okay, go!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.060
L-Let's go, Victories...

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:08.730
Louder! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:10.550
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:16.010
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, 
Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.270
<i>So this is what she meant.</i>

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.260
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.260
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:24.990
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.520
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.830
Let's go, Victories!

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:32.250
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, 
Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.020
<i>That girl's voice is so loud...</i>

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:32.650
<i>You're amazing, Senpai!</i>

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:37.690
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, 
Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:43.120
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, 
Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.730
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:50.630
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.110
<i>I-I cheered with everything I had.</i>

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:56.320
<i>To liven up our halftime, we have</i>

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.730
<i>the Kaminoki High School
 Cheerleading Squad!</i>

00:17:58.730 --> 00:17:59.300
Huh?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.840
<i>Let's love each other a little more</i>

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:15.230
<i>Everyone's got a lot on their plates</i>

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:18.560
<i>But it's a wonderful thing</i>

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:22.000
<i>There are times where you're 
just going to get hurt</i>

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.540
<i>But they've been cheering this whole time.</i>

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:26.460
<i>There are things you just can't beat</i>

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:29.330
<i>But I want to stay by your side!</i>

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:32.470
<i>They're dancing like they're totally fine...</i>

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:36.480
<i>He's a 27-year-old editor who's aspiring</i>

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.930
<i>To become a writer someday</i>

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.380
<i>Actually, no. They're half-exhausted.</i>

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.080
<i>I work at a travel agency</i>

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:47.310
<i>And I've come to see people 
off again at Narita</i>

00:18:47.710 --> 00:19:00.110
<i>I don't think we've seen each other 
since Ichiro hit that grand slam home run</i>

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:08.790
<i>Soon, I won't even be able 
to remember your face</i>

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:12.350
<i>Let's love each other a little more</i>

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:15.420
<i>Everyone's got a lot on their plates</i>

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.510
<i>But it's a wonderful thing</i>

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.260
<i>There are times where you're 
just going to get hurt</i>

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:26.890
<i>There are a lot of things 
you just can't beat</i>

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:32.150
<i>But I just want to stay by your side</i>

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.620
Sawatari, good job cheering earlier.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:37.150
Huh?

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:39.610
All right, you'll be starting 
in the second half.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:40.900
Y-Yes, sir!

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.320
<i>They were cheering the whole time, 
and then they did that dance.</i>

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.540
<i>There's no way they're totally fine.</i>

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:55.780
Let's go, Victories! Let's go, Victories!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.550
<b>Fires                         Victories</b>

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.550
<b>First Half

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.360
Akane!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.950
Thanks for everything today.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:55.640
No, thank you. It's just like we heard.

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.210
Those girls do bring good luck.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.300
Luck?

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.020
Yes.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:01.440
They say when you ask the girls of 
Kaminoki High to cheer for you,

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:02.920
you'll be sure to win.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:04.340
Ah...

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.540
S-Sis...

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:10.090
So, um, today, um...

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:13.120
We could've won without your cheers,

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.750
but, uh, I guess we should thank you anyway.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.200
Aw, he's being shy.

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.250
He's definitely Uki-chan's little brother.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.330
Also, uh, I thought...

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:25.470
cheerleading is really cool!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.790
Huh?

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.740
Congrats, Akki!

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:34.730
You all worked so hard! You were great!

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:36.640
Shut up, Kohane!

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:37.980
Don't call me Akki!

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.670
That shot was really cool!

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.730
It made me want to cheer even harder!

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:46.440
Yeah, well, I know you guys were 
exhausted in the second half!

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.120
Huh? You knew?

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:51.490
And that outfit doesn't 
look good on you at all!

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:53.120
Aw, you're being shy.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:55.750
You're really just like Uki.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.460
I'm not being shy!

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:00.080
What the heck?

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.340
You're so cute!

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:01.340
Shut up!

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:04.340
You two really are alike.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:06.120
Stop it!

